  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">5 MW Solar Photovoltaic (PV) and 30 MW PV Hybrid Power Plants, through Power Engineers, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A USTDA grant in support of Solar Era Holdings Limited to fund a feasibility study to assess the technical, financial and economic viability of a five megawatt (MW) solar photovoltaic power plant as well as a planned second phase expansion to a 30 MW solar hybrid plant near Bo, the second largest city in Sierra Leone. The study will provide the grantee with information and analyses that offer a blueprint for implementing both phases of the project on a commercially and technically viable basis. This project would bring badly needed energy into the grid in Sierra Leone, where at present only 13 percent of the population has access to electricity.</narrative>
  </description>
